# `@SquirrelJMEVendorApi` and `@KeepWhenCompacting` Cleanup (Done)

With the ProGuard changes there are cases where `@SquirrelJMEVendorApi` was
added to prevent it from removing a class, which no longer has an effect for
private and package-private. For those cases where it is needed,
then `@KeepWhenCompacting` should be used. Otherwise, it should be removed
completely.

Additionally, `@SquirrelJMEVendorApi` should only be used on APIs that are
intended to be used by vendors and end-users who want to use specific
SquirrelJME features, and _not_ public implementations of specific services
or utilities. An example where it would not apply would be an implementation
of `Connection`, it needs a `@KeepWhenCompacting` so it is not removed for
`ServiceLoader` usage however it can be compacted to reduce space usage. This
also applies for cases where there are native callbacks from the MLE layer
called to a class, it is appropriate to use `@KeepWhenCompacting`.

