## Resultant Solution

The ProGuard rules were redone to effectively never shrink, ProGuard's term
for removing classes, and only optimize and obfuscate. This means that there
is now never a worry for a class being deleted. What followed was effectively
going through ProGuard's set of optimizations, each likely one that would break
code would be flipped and SpringCoat Release would be run to ensure that it
still runs the launcher and reaches the main list. The mystify and hello
demos were also run to ensure that this operated correctly. This took about
four days on and off.

Once everything worked, removing the debug code required more optimizations
to be flipped, naturally being checked to make sure everything still ran. The
check for debugging was also turned into a method as some `javac` compilers
seem to inline static fields and otherwise; or ProGuard seems to just have an
easier time overall if a method is called rather than a field being accessed.
This removes virtually all debugging output, which results in slightly smaller
code sizes.

Note that class and member names are still always unique and that type clashing
has been specifically disabled in ProGuard. Although this slightly does
reduce the ability to make everything smaller, it does allow for better
debugging for release builds along with more sane stack traces. I would rather
have that than smaller code. It also is easier to figure out exactly which
method is being called as well.

Thus from all of this, `@SquirrelJMEVendorApi` and `@KeepWhenCompacting` are
no longer needed and thus have been deleted.

There is now `@KeepAbsolutelyEverything` to force ProGuard to keep everything
for a specific class. This is only set at the top of the class level and
affects all members so it only needs to be specified once.

For reference, the initial classes to be flagged are as followed for the
given reason:

 * `AccessController` -- "Security".
 * `Boolean` -- Boxed type.
 * `Byte` -- Boxed type.
 * `Character` -- Boxed type.
 * `Double` -- Boxed type.
 * `Float` -- Boxed type.
 * `Integer` -- Boxed type.
 * `Long` -- Boxed type.
 * `Permission` -- "Security".
 * `PermissionCollection` -- "Security".
 * `Runtime` -- VM internals are needed by SpringCoat/NanoCoat.
 * `SecurityManager` -- "Security".
 * `Short` -- Boxed type.
 * `System` -- VM internals are needed by SpringCoat/NanoCoat.
 * `Thread` -- VM internals are needed by SpringCoat/NanoCoat.
 * `Throwable` -- VM internals are needed by SpringCoat/NanoCoat.
 * `__AppLaunch__` -- Main entry point.
 * `__MainHandler__` -- Main entry point.
 * `__StarAppLaunch__` -- Main entry point.
 * `__Start__` -- Main entry point.
